mailo:EPO_G0001_19 a mailo:EPOProceding ;
    rdfs:label "EPO G 0001/19 — Patentability of Computer-Implemented Simulations"@en ;
    dcterms:date "2021-03-10"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:identifier "G 0001/19" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (TransposedPrinciple): Computer-implemented simulation generally. MAILO applies the technical-character reasoning to clinical simulation; the Enlarged Board did not rule on medical AI."@en ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:EPO_EnlargedBoA ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:TransposedPrinciple ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Computer-implemented simulation of a technical process is not excluded from patentability (Art.52(2)). Technical character assessed at claim level. Foundational for AI-based clinical decision simulation systems."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:interpretesArticle mailo:EPC_Art52 .

mailo:EPO_T1191_19 a mailo:EPOProceding ;
    rdfs:label "EPO T 1191/19 — Neuronal plasticity/INSTITUT GUTTMANN: meta-learning, inventive step and training-data sufficiency"@en ;
    dcterms:date "2022-04-01"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:identifier "T 1191/19" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Meta-learning for personalised neurorehabilitation interventions."@en ;
    mailo:citesPrecedent mailo:EPO_T0161_18 ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:EPO_BoA ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:DirectSubjectMatter ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Technical Board of Appeal 3.5.05, application 08877672.9 (Fundacio Institut Guttmann): computer-implemented meta-learning method predicting personalised neurorehabilitation interventions. Appeal dismissed. Art.56: the mere application of a known machine learning technique to problems in a particular field is a general trend in technology (following T 161/18 point 3.6) and cannot be inventive as such. Art.83: insufficient disclosure - no example training or validation data, no minimum patient number for a meaningful prediction, and no disclosure of the artificial neural networks' topology, activation functions, end conditions or learning mechanism (following T 161/18 point 2); the Board described the disclosure as more like an invitation to a research programme. Separately, late-filed documents AX2-AX8 were not admitted under RPBA Art.12(4) - an evidential admissibility ruling, NOT a plausibility holding."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:interpretesArticle mailo:EPC_Art56,
        mailo:EPC_Art83,
        mailo:EPC_Art84 .

