mailo:Risk_TradeSecretTransparencyConflict a mailo:ComplianceRisk ;
    rdfs:label "Trade Secret Shield vs. AI Act/GDPR Transparency Mandate (TSD Art.2 Conflict)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Medical AI operators relying on TSD Art.2 to protect model weights face: (a) mandatory AI Act Art.13 disclosure to deployers; (b) GDPR Art.15(1)(h) actionable explanation obligations to data subjects; (c) mandatory supervisory authority adjudication when TSD is claimed (C-203/22). Hybrid strategy required: patent final outputs, trade secret the AI platform, use ZKP/ZKML for auditor verification without weight disclosure."@en ;
    mailo:mitigatedBy mailo:ExplainabilityObligation ;
    mailo:riskLevel "HIGH"^^xsd:string .

mailo:Sanofi a mailo:Company ;
    rdfs:label "Sanofi S.A."@en .

mailo:SoftwareAsMedicalDevice a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "SoftwareAsMedicalDevice",
        "Software as Medical Device (SaMD)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Software qualifying as medical device under MDR 2017/745",
        "Software qualifying as a medical device under MDR 2017/745."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso airo:HighRiskAISystem ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mailo:MedicalAISystem ;
    mailo:hasRisk mailo:Risk_AIActQMS_MDR_Overlap,
        mailo:Risk_SEP_FRAND .

mailo:Tension_BlackBox_PatentProtection a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "Black-Box Patent Protection vs. EU AI Act Transparency Obligation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """\r
        Deep-learning medical AI is inherently opaque (black-box). Patent protection incentivises\r
        secrecy over model weights. EU AI Act Art.13 and C-817/19 black-box prohibition\r
        require transparency for high-risk AI systems, creating structural tension with\r
        commercial IP protection strategies. TSD Art.2 reinforces the secrecy interest;\r
        TSD Art.5 carve-outs are the only legislative bridge, but their scope is unresolved.\r
    """@en ;
    mailo:conflictsWith mailo:TransparencyObligation ;
    mailo:involvesFramework mailo:AIAct,
        mailo:EPC,
        mailo:TSD .

mailo:Tension_DGA_Neutrality_DataAcquisition a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "DGA Art.10 neutrality obligation vs. AI Act Art.10 data governance"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "DGA Art.10 prohibits data-sharing intermediaries from using shared data for purposes beyond the sharing service. Integrated AI development models in which intermediary and developer are related entities require structural business model restructuring that no guidance resolves."@en ;
    mailo:conflictType mailo:DataGovernanceConflict ;
    mailo:hasResolutionStatus "unresolved"^^xsd:string .

mailo:Tension_DataAct_TradeSecret_AITransparency a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "Data Act Art.15 trade secret vs. AI Act Art.13 + GDPR Art.15(1)(h) transparency"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "C-203/22 Dun & Bradstreet §§60-70 limits trade-secret defence: a controller cannot refuse all causal explanation on trade-secret grounds. The precise boundary between permitted limitation and impermissible derogation is determined case-by-case."@en ;
    mailo:conflictType mailo:TradeSecretConflict ;
    mailo:hasResolutionStatus "partial"^^xsd:string .

mailo:Tension_EHDS_GDPR_OptOut a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "EHDS Art.35 opt-out vs. AI Act Art.10(3) representativeness"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "EHDS Art.35 grants patients an unconditional right to opt out of secondary health data use. Where opt-out rates are elevated in a clinically significant subpopulation, the resulting training dataset violates AI Act Art.10(3) representativeness. No legislative safe harbour bridges these positions."@en ;
    mailo:conflictType mailo:DataGovernanceConflict ;
    mailo:hasResolutionStatus "unresolved"^^xsd:string .

mailo:Tension_EPO_GDPR_Disclosure a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "EPC Art.83 Sufficiency Disclosure vs. GDPR Art.15(1)(h) + TSD Art.2 Secrecy"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """\r
        EPC Art.83 requires public disclosure of training data structure to maintain patent validity.\r
        GDPR Art.15(1)(h) + C-203/22 require actionable explanations to data subjects.\r
        The EPO disclosure may inadvertently establish a baseline that strengthens GDPR access rights,\r
        eroding TSD Art.2 trade secret shields that might otherwise limit GDPR Art.15 responses.\r
        TSD Art.9 judicial confidentiality measures do not apply to EPO prosecution, leaving no\r
        mechanism to contain the disclosure baseline once it enters the public patent record.\r
    """@en ;
    mailo:conflictsWith mailo:DisclosureObligation ;
    mailo:involvesFramework mailo:EPC,
        mailo:GDPR,
        mailo:TSD .

mailo:Tension_EPO_MDR_SemanticScope a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "EPO G-II §3.3 broad claim scope vs. MDR Annex II §1.1 + AI Act Art.9/13 intended purpose"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "EPO patent prosecution optimises for broad technical-effect claims (wider scope = stronger IP protection); MDR Annex II requires precise intended-purpose specification (narrower scope = easier clinical evaluation); AI Act Art.9/13 requires intermediate characterisation covering intended purpose plus reasonably foreseeable misuse. The same SaMD must be described at opposing granularity levels across three institutional knowledge spaces. No EPO, MDCG, or AI Office guidance addresses this triangular scope alignment problem."@en ;
    mailo:conflictType mailo:SemanticGranularityConflict ;
    mailo:hasResolutionStatus "unresolved"^^xsd:string .

mailo:Tension_MDR_AIAct_DualTrack a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "MDR Annex IX conformity vs. AI Act Art.43 conformity assessment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Two separate conformity assessment pathways for the same SaMD. MDCG AIB 2025-1 provides a procedural joint-assessment mechanism but does not harmonise the substantive requirement sets."@en ;
    mailo:conflictType mailo:ConformityGapConflict ;
    mailo:hasResolutionStatus "procedural_only"^^xsd:string .

mailo:Tension_PLD_AIAct_Liability a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "PLD Strict Liability vs. AI Act Conformity Defence"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """\r
        PLD Art.5 imposes strict liability; AI Act conformity assessment is not a\r
        defence to PLD claims. A CE-marked AI-SaMD that passes AI Act conformity\r
        assessment may still be 'defective' under PLD if it fails in real-world\r
        deployment. The two regimes do not create a safety harbour from each other.\r
    """@en ;
    mailo:conflictsWith mailo:PLD_Art5 .

mailo:Tension_PLD_AIAct_LiabilityGap a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "PLD Art.10 defect presumption vs. AI Act Art.9 risk management"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "PLD Art.10 defect presumption applies where it is excessively difficult for the claimant to prove defect. AI Act Art.9-compliant risk management documentation may rebut the presumption but no legislative safe harbour confirms this."@en ;
    mailo:conflictType mailo:LiabilityConflict ;
    mailo:hasResolutionStatus "partial"^^xsd:string .

mailo:Tension_TSD_AIAct_Transparency a mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:label "TSD Art.2 Trade Secret vs. AI Act Art.13 + GDPR Art.15(1)(h) — Core Transparency Tension"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "TSD Art.2 protects model weights, training data schemas, and architecture as trade secrets. AI Act Art.13 requires deployers to receive sufficient information about high-risk AI system capabilities and limitations. C-203/22 §§60-70 sets the mandatory floor: controller cannot invoke TSD Art.2 to deny all causal explanation of an automated decision — disputed information must be produced to the competent supervisory authority or court for balance. AI Act Art.78 ensures national authority confidentiality but does not disapply Art.13 disclosure to deployers. TSD Art.5 is the only legislative bridge but its scope in the medical AI context remains unresolved pending a CJEU reference on Art.22 and clinical AI."@en ;
    mailo:conflictType mailo:TradeSecretConflict ;
    mailo:conflictsWith mailo:ExplainabilityObligation,
        mailo:TransparencyObligation ;
    mailo:hasResolutionStatus "partial"^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:involvesFramework mailo:AIAct,
        mailo:GDPR,
        mailo:TSD .

mailo:TimelineEvent a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "TimelineEvent" ;
    rdfs:comment "A regulatory obligation activation date or deadline" .

mailo:UPCA a mailo:InternationalTreaty,
        mailo:RegulatoryFramework ;
    rdfs:label "UPC Agreement (UPCA)"@en ;
    dcterms:date "2023-06-01"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:identifier "OJ C 175, 20.6.2013" ;
    rdfs:comment "Agreement on a Unified Patent Court (in force 2023-06-01). Establishes the UPC as a supranational court for infringement and revocation of European patents across contracting states. Key for medtech AI: opt-out strategy, PI threshold ('more likely than not' invalidity standard from 10x v. NanoString CoA), EPO-UPC divergence risk."@en .

mailo:UPC_10x_NanoString a mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:label "10x Genomics v. NanoString — Spatial Biology AI"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Spatial genomic analysis instrumentation and methods."@en ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:UPC_CoA,
        mailo:UPC_LD_Munich ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:DirectSubjectMatter ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Munich LD granted PI; CoA first substantive ruling reversed PI on invalidity grounds ('more likely than not' standard). Case settled 2025."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:hasStatus "Settled 2025"^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:involvesTechnology mailo:GenomicDiagnosticAI .

mailo:UPC_Dexcom_Abbott a mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:label "Dexcom v. Abbott — Continuous Glucose Monitoring"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "ACT_583778/2023" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Continuous glucose monitoring with algorithmic estimation."@en ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:UPC_LD_Munich,
        mailo:UPC_LD_Paris ;
    mailo:hasDefendant mailo:Abbott ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:DirectSubjectMatter ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Paris LD revoked EP 3435866 and EP 3831282 (EPO had maintained validity — divergence). Case settled Dec 2024."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:hasPlaintiff mailo:Dexcom ;
    mailo:hasStatus "Settled 2024-12-20"^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:involvesTechnology mailo:RiskScoringSystem .

mailo:UPC_GXD_Myriad a mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:label "GXD-Bio v. Myriad Genetics — Genomic Diagnostic AI"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "UPC_CFI_437/2024" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Genomic diagnostic signature patent (EndoPredict)."@en ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:UPC_LD_Munich ;
    mailo:hasDefendant mailo:MyriadGenetics ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:DirectSubjectMatter ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Munich Local Division, December 2025: EP 3 346 403 revoked for added matter and the infringement claims against Myriad's EndoPredict test dismissed. First UPC biotech NPE action."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:hasPlaintiff mailo:GXDBio ;
    mailo:hasStatus "Under appeal — GXD-Bio appealed in February 2026 (verified 2026-09-01)"^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:involvesPatent mailo:EP_3346403 ;
    mailo:involvesTechnology mailo:GenomicDiagnosticAI .

mailo:UPC_Hologic_Siemens a mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:label "Hologic v. Siemens Healthineers — Medical Imaging AI"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "UPC_CFI_758/2024" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (DomainContext): Mammography X-ray tube hardware, with no AI element in the asserted claim. Retained only for the EPO/MDR semantic-scope tension, where the point is precisely that patent claim scope and MDR intended purpose describe the same device at different granularities."@en,
        "SCOPE WARNING: this is medical imaging HARDWARE (X-ray tube focal spot control), not medical imaging AI. The asserted claim contains no AI or machine-learning element. Retained for the EPO/MDR/AI Act semantic-scope tension analysis, but it should not be counted as a medical-AI patent case."@en ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:UPC_LD_Dusseldorf ;
    mailo:hasDefendant mailo:SiemensHealthineers ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:DomainContext ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Dusseldorf Local Division, decision of 10 June 2026 (with counterclaim UPC_CFI_259/2025): permanent injunction granted to Hologic in three member states, with recall and destruction orders against several Siemens Healthineers entities. The patent concerns the 'Flying Focal Spot' X-ray tube feature of the MAMMOMAT B.brilliant mammography system. NOTE: the item previously recorded here as a decision of 2026-03-09 was a procedural order on the further exchange of written pleadings, not the judgment."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:hasPlaintiff mailo:Hologic ;
    mailo:hasStatus "Decided at first instance 2026-06-10 (verified 2026-09-01)"^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:involvesPatent mailo:EP_2352431 .

mailo:UPC_Microsoft_Suinno a mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:label "Microsoft v. Suinno — AI Method Patent"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "UPC_CFI_433/2024" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (ProceduralPrecedent): EP 2 671 173 is a walking-and-browsing patent, neither medical nor AI. Retained for UPC practice only: Rule 30 RoP auxiliary requests and the representation requirement. Originally captured because the party name contains 'AI'."@en,
        "SCOPE WARNING: EP 2 671 173 is a 'method and means for browsing by walking' - discovering web search results by physical proximity while walking. It is neither a medical nor an AI patent. The party name (Suinno Mobile & AI Technologies Licensing Oy) contains 'AI', which is the likely reason this case was captured. It should not be counted as a medical-AI patent case."@en ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:UPC_CD_Paris ;
    mailo:hasDefendant mailo:Microsoft ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:ProceduralPrecedent ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Paris Central Division, 7 January 2026: EP 2 671 173 revoked in its entirety on the counterclaim for revocation, with extensive guidance on the admissibility and presentation of auxiliary requests under Rule 30 RoP. Separately, the Court of Appeal held that Suinno was not validly represented, its managing director and main shareholder being precluded from acting as its UPC representative despite being qualified. NOTE: the ground previously recorded here as 'added matter' has not been confirmed against the decision text."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:hasStatus "Revoked at first instance 2026-01-07; appealed by Suinno (verified 2026-09-01)"^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:involvesPatent mailo:EP_2671173 .

mailo:UPC_Sanofi_Amgen a mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:label "Sanofi & Regeneron v. Amgen — PCSK9 Medical Use"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "UPC_CFI_505/2024" ;
    rdfs:comment "Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Antibody claims; biologic rather than AI, retained for claim-scope reasoning."@en ;
    mailo:decidedBy mailo:UPC_LD_Dusseldorf ;
    mailo:hasInclusionBasis mailo:DirectSubjectMatter ;
    mailo:hasOutcome "Düsseldorf LD: patent valid, no infringement (dual-element test established). CoA: EP'797 restored after Munich CD revocation. EPO-UPC divergence on inventive step."^^xsd:string ;
    mailo:hasStatus "Active — EPO BoA hearing scheduled 2026-04"^^xsd:string .

mailo:amendmentDescription a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Human-readable description of what this legislative event changes" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:amendmentProcedureRef a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "amendment procedure reference"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The interinstitutional procedure file number, which is the stable handle for tracking status."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:PendingAmendment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:amendmentProposalRef a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "amendment proposal reference"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The Commission document reference of the proposal."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:PendingAmendment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:applicablePhase a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Named applicability phase label (e.g. 'high_risk_full_obligations')" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:applicationDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Date from which the act applies" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date .

mailo:appliesTo a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "applies to"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Principle applies to a technology" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalPrinciple ;
    rdfs:range mailo:Technology .

mailo:art22ExceptionApplied a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Art.22 exception applied"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "contract_necessity | explicit_consent | member_state_law",
        "The GDPR Art.22(2) exception relied on: 'contract_necessity' | 'explicit_consent' | 'member_state_law'. Must be stated or Art.22(1) prohibition applies (C-634/21 P_634_004)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:caseDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Date of judgment or decision" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date .

mailo:celex a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "CELEX number for EU legislation" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:chamberType a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Grand Chamber, Chamber, etc." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:cites a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Cites another CJEU case (alias)" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CJEUCase ;
    rdfs:range mailo:CJEUCase .

mailo:citesPrecedent a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "cites precedent"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Case relies on earlier case as precedent",
        "A case relies on an earlier case as precedent."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:Case .

mailo:complementedBy a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "complemented by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Article is complemented by another" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalArticle .

mailo:conflictType a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "conflict type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Relates a CrossFrameworkTension to the kind of conflict it exhibits. Declared in v5.1.0."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:range mailo:ConflictType .

mailo:conflictsWith a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "conflicts with"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Article conflicts with another",
        "Two legal obligations or principles that are in tension."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalArticle .

mailo:coversArticle a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "covers article"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Framework contains an article" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:RegulatoryFramework ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalArticle .

mailo:decidedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "decided by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Case was decided by a court" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:Court .

mailo:discusses a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Source discusses a legal principle" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalPrinciple .

mailo:doi a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Digital Object Identifier" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:ecliIdentifier a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "ECLI case identifier" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:enforcedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Framework enforced by authority" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:RegulatoryFramework ;
    rdfs:range mailo:RegulatoryAuthority .

mailo:entryIntoForce a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Date of entry into force" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date .

mailo:establishesPrinciple a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "establishes principle"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Case establishes a legal principle",
        "A case establishes a legal principle."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalPrinciple .

mailo:governedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Governed by a regulatory framework" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Technology ;
    rdfs:range mailo:RegulatoryFramework .

mailo:grantsRight a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "grants right"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Article grants a right" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:range mailo:Right .

mailo:hasConformityRecord a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has conformity record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links system to its conformity record" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:MedicalAISystem ;
    rdfs:range mailo:ConformityRecord .

mailo:hasDPIA a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has DPIA"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links system to its DPIA record",
        "Links a medical AI system to its DPIA record. Required for all high-risk automated processing (GDPR Art.35; C-817/19 P_817_005)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:MedicalAISystem ;
    rdfs:range mailo:DPIARecord .

mailo:hasDefendant a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has defendant"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Defendant in the case" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalEntity .

mailo:hasDefinedScope a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has defined scope"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Tri-level proportionality (a): targeted scope (C-817/19 P_817_003)",
        "Tri-level proportionality test (a): targeted scope. C-817/19 P_817_003."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:hasEncodingBasis a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has encoding basis"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Distinguishes a court's holding from the designer's operationalisation or transposition of it. Required on every encoded principle."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalPrinciple ;
    rdfs:range mailo:EncodingBasis .

mailo:hasExplanation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has explanation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links system to its explanation for data subjects",
        "Links an automated decision system to its actionable explanation for data subjects (C-203/22 P_203_001; GDPR Art.15(1)(h))."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range mailo:Explanation .

mailo:hasFormation a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "court formation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CJEUCase ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:hasHumanOversightRecord a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has human oversight record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links system to its oversight documentation",
        "Links an automated decision system to its human oversight documentation. At least one record is required (C-634/21 P_634_002)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range mailo:HumanOversightRecord .

mailo:hasInclusionBasis a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has inclusion basis"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Records why a case belongs in MAILO. Required on every Case; see mailo:InclusionBasisShape."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:InclusionBasis .

mailo:hasIndividualNonAutomatedReview a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has individual non-automated review"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "True = individual non-automated review before any measure (C-817/19 P_817_001)",
        "True if every positive automated match is subject to individual non-automated human review before any measure is taken. C-817/19 P_817_001 constitutional minimum."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:hasObligation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Framework imposes an obligation" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:RegulatoryFramework ;
    rdfs:range mailo:ComplianceObligation .

mailo:hasOutcome a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "outcome"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Outcome or operative part of judgment" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:hasPendingAmendment a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has pending amendment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links a LegalArticle whose numbering or content is currently in force to a proposed amendment that has not been adopted. Asserting this property makes no claim that the amendment will pass."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:range mailo:PendingAmendment .

mailo:hasPlaintiff a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has plaintiff"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Plaintiff in the case" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalEntity .

mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "precedence level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "binding_ratio | persuasive_obiter | constitutional_grand_chamber | authorial_transposition",
        "binding_ratio | persuasive_obiter | constitutional_grand_chamber | authorial_transposition. The first three record how much interpretive weight a holding claims. The fourth marks a mapping the ontology designer has drawn across instruments or contexts, which is NOT a holding of the Court and must not be cited as one. This is an analytical metadata model adopted by MAILO, not a formal precedent hierarchy operated by the CJEU."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalPrinciple ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:hasPredeterminedCriteria a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has predetermined criteria"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "True = pre-determined explainable criteria; false = self-learning black-box",
        "True if the system's assessment criteria are pre-determined and not modified by self-learning without human review. Required to avoid black-box prohibition (C-817/19 P_817_002)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:hasPrinciple a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Establishes a legal principle (alias)" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CJEUCase ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalPrinciple .

mailo:hasPurposeLimitation a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has purpose limitation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Tri-level proportionality (b): purpose limitation",
        "Tri-level proportionality test (b): documented purpose limitation. C-817/19 P_817_003."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:hasResolutionStatus a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has resolution status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Records whether the tension between two frameworks has been resolved by legislation, case law or authoritative guidance. Values in use: 'unresolved' (no authority addresses the conflict), 'partial' (addressed in part, or addressed for an analogous but not identical situation), and 'procedural_only' (an authority routes the conflict to a forum without fixing a substantive outcome, as in C-203/22). This records the state of the law, not the ontology designer's confidence. Declared in v5.1.0 Round 5: the property was in use on tension instances but had never been typed or defined, so its value set was undocumented and unqueryable."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:hasRisk a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has compliance risk"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Technology carries a compliance risk" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Technology ;
    rdfs:range mailo:ComplianceRisk .

mailo:hasStatus a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Procedural status of the case" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:hasTemporalLimitation a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has temporal limitation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Tri-level proportionality (c): temporal limitation or review schedule",
        "Tri-level proportionality test (c): temporal limitation or mandatory periodic review. C-817/19 P_817_003."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:hasTension a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Tension involves a framework" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:range mailo:RegulatoryFramework .

mailo:hasVersion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Regulation has a temporal applicability version" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:EURegulation ;
    rdfs:range mailo:RegulationVersion .

mailo:identifiesInputFactors a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "identifies input factors"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Explanation identifies which inputs affected the output",
        "True if the explanation identifies which specific input data affected the automated output and the main reasoning path (C-203/22 P_203_001; GDPR Art.15(1)(h))."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Explanation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:interpretesArticle a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "interprets article"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalArticle .

mailo:interpretsArticle a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Case interprets a specific article" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalArticle .

mailo:involvesFramework a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "involves framework"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A cross-framework tension involves a regulatory framework." ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CrossFrameworkTension ;
    rdfs:range mailo:RegulatoryFramework .

mailo:involvesPatent a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "involves patent"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "UPC case involves a patent" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:range mailo:Patent .

mailo:involvesTechnology a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "involves technology"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Case involves a technology class" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Case ;
    rdfs:range mailo:Technology .

mailo:ipcClass a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "IPC/CPC patent classification code" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:isActionable a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is actionable"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Explanation enables effective Art.22(3) remedies (C-203/22 P_203_001)",
        "True if the explanation enables effective exercise of GDPR Art.22(3) remedies (C-203/22 P_203_001). Abstract mathematical formulas are insufficient."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Explanation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:isCurrentVersion a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "True if this is the currently applicable version as of the query date" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:isHighRiskAIAct a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is high-risk under AI Act"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "True if system falls under AI Act Annex III high-risk categories",
        "True if the system falls within AI Act Annex III high-risk categories (medical device AI, biometric, critical infrastructure)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:MedicalAISystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:isNonTechnical a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is non-technical"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Explanation expressed in non-technical language",
        "True if the explanation is expressed in language understandable to the data subject without specialist knowledge (C-203/22 P_203_001)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Explanation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:legislativeStatus a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "legislative status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Stage reached in the ordinary legislative procedure at the date given by statusVerifiedAsAt. Values used: 'proposed', 'council_position', 'parliament_position', 'trilogue', 'provisional_agreement', 'adopted'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:PendingAmendment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:lit_Andrade_F_Rebelo_D_M_2024_Schufa_s_Case_C-634_21_on a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Andrade, F., Rebelo, D. M. (2024). Schufa's Case C-634/21 on ADM: the 'Lenders' Quest' for GDPR-friendly Scoring has not been settled yet! SSRN 4882806." ;
    dcterms:date "2024" ;
    dcterms:description "Challenges the breadth of SCHUFA holding. Informs MAILO's functional-solely rule encoding." ;
    dcterms:source <https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4882806> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 4 .

mailo:lit_Communications_Medicine_Nature_2025_Neuro-symbolic_AI a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Communications Medicine (Nature). (2025). Neuro-symbolic AI for auditable cognitive information extraction from medical reports." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "LLM extracts candidate facts → symbolic verifier checks against medical rules → traceable, deterministic labels. Empirical demonstration of the harness pattern MAILO advocates, applied to clinical text." ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.nature.com/articles/s43856-025-01194-x> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_Conflict-tolerant_Deontic_Traditional_Scheme_for_the_Semanti a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Conflict-tolerant Deontic Traditional Scheme for the Semantic Web. (2025). Journal of Logic and Computation 35(8), Oxford." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "Addresses cross-framework normative conflict resolution that MAILO will face (e.g. GDPR Art.22 vs AI Act Art.86). Provides RDF-based conflict-tolerant deontic logic." ;
    dcterms:source <https://academic.oup.com/logcom/article/35/8/exaf054/8320660> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 4 .

mailo:lit_DAOnt_A_Formal_Ontology_for_EU_Data_Act_Compliance_2024_2 a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "DAOnt: A Formal Ontology for EU Data Act Compliance. (2024/2026). arXiv:2604.16386." ;
    dcterms:date "2024" ;
    dcterms:description "Reuses LKIF-Core + ODRL + DPV. Single-framework analogue of MAILO's multi-framework target." ;
    dcterms:source <https://arxiv.org/html/2604.16386> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 4 .

mailo:lit_EHJ_Digital_Health_Oxford_2025_Medicine_healthcare_an a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "EHJ Digital Health (Oxford). (2025). Medicine, healthcare and the AI act: gaps, challenges and future implications." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "Explicit multi-framework gap analysis. Core citation for MAILO Chapter 2." ;
    dcterms:source <https://academic.oup.com/ehjdh/advance-article/doi/10.1093/ehjdh/ztaf041/8118685> ;
