mailo:lit_Esteves_B_Rodr_guez-Doncel_V_et_al_2024_Analysis_of a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Esteves, B., Rodríguez-Doncel, V. et al. (2024). Analysis of ontologies and policy languages to represent information flows in GDPR. Semantic Web Journal." ;
    dcterms:date "2024" ;
    dcterms:description "Comparative table of ontology and policy languages. Positions DPV + ODRL + LegalRuleML as Pareto-front. ODRL+LegalRuleML+DPV+GDPRtEXT can model 39 of 57 informational items." ;
    dcterms:source <https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.3233/SW-223009> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 4 .

mailo:lit_Frontiers_Digital_Health_2025_Ontologies_as_the_semantic a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Frontiers Digital Health. (2025). Ontologies as the semantic bridge between artificial intelligence and healthcare." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "OWL2 + SWRL semantic reasoning enables auditable inference consistent with domain expertise. Ontologies encode explicit rules and traceable data relationships required by AI Act. Doctrinal scaffold for MAILO." ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/digital-health/articles/10.3389/fdgth.2025.1668385/full> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_Golpayegani_D_Pandit_H_J_Lewis_D_2022_2025_AIRO a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Golpayegani, D., Pandit, H. J., Lewis, D. (2022, 2025). AIRO: An Ontology for Representing AI Risks Based on the Proposed EU AI Act. SEMANTiCS + arXiv:2501.10391." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "OWL ontology + SHACL shapes implementing AI Act Annex III high-risk classifier + SPARQL ASK queries; integrated into W3C DPVCG. Most direct competitor to MAILO. AIRO already does for the AI Act what MAILO proposes for the medical-AI multi-framework intersection. Differentiator: MAILO adds medical-domain specificity, MDR+PLD integration, CJEU precedent chain, UPC patent overlay." ;
    dcterms:source <https://delaramglp.github.io/airo/> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_Hybrid_Neuro-Symbolic_Models_for_Ethical_AI_in_Risk-Sensitiv a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Hybrid Neuro-Symbolic Models for Ethical AI in Risk-Sensitive Domains. (2025). arXiv:2511.17644." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "Risk-sensitive domains demand transparency + regulatory compliance. Neural pattern recognition + symbolic reasoning yields verifiable explanations. Healthcare among the case studies." ;
    dcterms:source <https://arxiv.org/html/2511.17644v1> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_JMIR_2026_The_Right_to_Understand_in_Health_Care_AI a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "JMIR. (2026). The Right to Understand in Health Care AI." ;
    dcterms:date "2026" ;
    dcterms:description "Argues neither AI Act nor GDPR specifies what a meaningful clinical explanation is. Identifies the gap MAILO fills via its semantic schema." ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.jmir.org/2026/1/e95090> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_Kang_M_Li_B_et_al_2025_R_-Guard_Robust_Reasoning_E a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Kang, M., Li, B. et al. (2025). R²-Guard: Robust Reasoning Enabled LLM Guardrail via Knowledge-Enhanced Logical Reasoning. ICLR 2025." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "Markov logic networks + probabilistic circuits over a safety reasoning graph. +30.2% over Llama Guard on ToxicChat; +59.5% under jailbreak attacks. Direct precedent for logic-graph-as-runtime-safety-filter pattern that MAILO advances, but for general LLM safety, not medical regulation." ;
    dcterms:source <https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.05557> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_MDCG_2025-6_2025_European_Commission_Joint_Guidance_on_M a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "MDCG 2025-6. (2025). European Commission Joint Guidance on MDR/IVDR × AI Act." ;
    dcterms:date "2025" ;
    dcterms:description "Official EU-level mapping document. MAILO instances must align with it." ;
    dcterms:source <https://health.ec.europa.eu/document/download/b78a17d7-e3cd-4943-851d-e02a2f22bbb4_en> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_MDPI_Information_2024_A_SHACL-Based_Approach_for_Enhanci a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "MDPI Information. (2024). A SHACL-Based Approach for Enhancing Automated Compliance Checking with RDF Data, 15(12):759." ;
    dcterms:date "2024" ;
    dcterms:description "Operationalises the validation layer that MAILO needs for runtime SHACL checks." ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.mdpi.com/2078-2489/15/12/759> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 4 .

mailo:lit_Medical_Law_Review_2024_A_health-conformant_reading_of_t a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Medical Law Review. (2024). A health-conformant reading of the GDPR's right not to be subject to automated decision-making, 32(3), 373." ;
    dcterms:date "2024" ;
    dcterms:description "Only article addressing the exact intersection of GDPR Art.22 + medical AI. Doctrinal foundation for MAILO's medical-AI ADM rules." ;
    dcterms:source <https://academic.oup.com/medlaw/article/32/3/373/7732100> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_Pandit_H_J_et_al_2024_Data_Privacy_Vocabulary_DPV a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Pandit, H. J. et al. (2024). Data Privacy Vocabulary (DPV) – Version 2.0. Springer / W3C DPVCG." ;
    dcterms:date "2024" ;
    dcterms:description "RDFS/SKOS + OWL2 alt; 911 concepts; serialised in TTL/JSON-LD/RDF-XML; namespace http://w3id.org/dpv#. Foundational vocabulary the thesis should reuse. Recommendation: import DPV namespace into MAILO; align mailo:hasObligation with dpv:hasLegalBasis." ;
    dcterms:source <https://w3c.github.io/dpv/2.1/dpv/> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_Rebedea_T_et_al_2023_NeMo_Guardrails_A_Toolkit_for_Co a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Rebedea, T. et al. (2023). NeMo Guardrails: A Toolkit for Controllable and Safe LLM Applications with Programmable Rails. EMNLP Demo. arXiv:2310.10501." ;
    dcterms:date "2023" ;
    dcterms:description "Colang DSL + dialogue-state engine; rules user-defined and interpretable. 2025 update: NIM micro-services with ~0.5s added latency for ~50% protection lift. Establishes programmable-rail paradigm; uses ad-hoc DSL not formal ontology." ;
    dcterms:source <https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.10501> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 4 .

mailo:lit_Robaldo_L_Bartolini_C_Palmirani_M_et_al_2020_Fo a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "Robaldo, L., Bartolini, C., Palmirani, M., et al. (2020). Formalizing GDPR Provisions in Reified I/O Logic: The DAPRECO Knowledge Base. Journal of Logic, Language and Information." ;
    dcterms:date "2020" ;
    dcterms:description "LegalRuleML + reified Input/Output logic + SPINDle defeasible reasoner. The canonical precedent for formal GDPR reasoning. Limitations addressed by MAILO: GDPR-only; no medical AI integration; no CJEU case-law layer; no runtime guardrail integration." ;
    dcterms:source <https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10849-019-09309-z> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 5 .

mailo:lit_npj_Health_Systems_2026_Data-driven_medical_devices_and a mailo:LiteratureSource ;
    rdfs:label "npj Health Systems. (2026). Data-driven medical devices and the EU MDR: mapping gaps in standards for regulatory compliance." ;
    dcterms:date "2026" ;
    dcterms:description "ISO/IEC 27001/27010 + ISO/IEC 5338, 25059, BS 30440 are insufficient for AI medical safety/transparency — exactly the gap MAILO addresses." ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.nature.com/articles/s44401-026-00075-2> ;
    mailo:relevanceScore 4 .

mailo:mitigatedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "mitigated by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Risk mitigated by obligation" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:ComplianceRisk ;
    rdfs:range mailo:ComplianceObligation .

mailo:overrules a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Overrules or modifies a prior principle" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:CJEUCase ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegalPrinciple .

mailo:oversightIsSubstantive a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "oversight is substantive"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "True = genuine review; false = rubber-stamping (C-634/21 P_634_002)",
        "True if the human reviewer exercised independent judgment; false if the review was a mere formality (rubber-stamping). C-634/21 P_634_002 requires true."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:HumanOversightRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:producesSignificantImpact a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "produces significant impact"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "True if outputs have legal/similarly significant effects on individuals",
        "True if the system's outputs have legal or similarly significant effects on individuals (C-634/21 P_634_001). Triggers full Art.22 obligation chain."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:proposedEffect a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "proposed effect"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "What the proposal would do to the provision, in the drafter's own terms."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:PendingAmendment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:proposedRenumberingTo a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "proposed renumbering to"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The article designation the provision would carry if the proposal is adopted as drafted. A string, not an IRI: the target provision does not exist in law and must not be resolvable as though it did."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:PendingAmendment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:relatedPatent a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Involves patent class" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:UPCCase ;
    rdfs:range mailo:PatentClassification .

mailo:relevanceScore a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Relevance score 1-5" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

mailo:requiresAssessment a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Technology requires a conformity path" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:Technology ;
    rdfs:range mailo:ConformityAssessment .

mailo:riskLevel a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "risk level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "CRITICAL | HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:ComplianceRisk ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mailo:statusVerifiedAsAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "status verified as at"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The date on which the legislative status recorded here was checked against a source. A status assertion without this date is not auditable and should not be relied on."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:PendingAmendment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date .

mailo:triggeredBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Version created or activated by a legislative event" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:RegulationVersion ;
    rdfs:range mailo:LegislativeAmendment .

mailo:triggersObligation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "triggers obligation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Principle triggers a compliance obligation" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:LegalPrinciple ;
    rdfs:range mailo:ComplianceObligation .

mailo:usesHealthStatusAsCriterion a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses health status as criterion"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Must be false — health status excluded from automated criteria (C-817/19 P_817_004)",
        "True if the system uses an individual's health status as an automated classification criterion. Must be false (C-817/19 P_817_004 Grand Chamber prohibition)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:AutomatedDecisionSystem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mailo:versionEndDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Date until which this version applies (exclusive; absent = open-ended)" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date .

mailo:versionOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Version belongs to a parent regulation" ;
    rdfs:domain mailo:RegulationVersion ;
    rdfs:range mailo:EURegulation .

mailo:versionStartDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Date from which this regulation version/expression applies" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date .

mailo:AIAct_Art10 a mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:label "AI Act Art.10 — Data Governance"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Training, validation, and test datasets for high-risk AI must meet quality criteria: relevance, representativeness, freedom from errors, completeness. Direct tension with data scarcity in rare disease AI."@en .

mailo:AIAct_Art17 a mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:label "AI Act Art.17 — Quality Management System"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "High-risk AI providers must implement a QMS covering design, development, post-market monitoring. Aligned with MDR Annex IX QMS requirements to avoid double burden."@en .

mailo:AIAct_Art26 a mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:label "AI Act Art.26 — Deployer Obligations"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Deployers (e.g., hospitals using third-party AI) must ensure human oversight, monitor performance, inform affected persons, maintain logs. Creates shared responsibility with providers."@en ;
    mailo:complementedBy mailo:AIAct_Art14 .

mailo:AIAct_Art50 a mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:label "AI Act Art.50 — Transparency obligations for certain AI systems"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Transparency duties on providers and deployers of AI systems that interact with natural persons or generate synthetic audio, image, video or text, including machine-readable marking and disclosure of artificially generated content. Applies to AI-generated radiology reports and diagnostic summaries. Relabelled in v5.1.0: this is NOT the GPAI regime, which is Chapter V (Arts.51-56) and addresses providers of general-purpose AI models."@en .

mailo:AIAct_Art9 a mailo:LegalArticle ;
    rdfs:label "AI Act Art.9 — Risk Management System"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "High-risk AI providers must establish and maintain a risk management system throughout the AI system lifecycle. Iterative process; complements MDR post-market surveillance."@en ;
    mailo:complementedBy mailo:AIAct_Art14 .

